# tools/ales_library_diff_witness.rish — what changed between two catalog versions: classify(before, after) sorts every album into
# added, removed, changed, or same (ALES229).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES229.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-143152_fill-ales229-lotus-library-diff.md
# Idiom kin: lotus/library_find.rye (ALES228, the find / digest_of resolve this composes on) · lotus/library_manifest.rye (ALES226,
# the two opened catalogs this compares). The first Lotus rung to stand ON another catalog primitive — no new hash, no new frame.
#
# lotus/library_diff.rye classifies two opened library manifests into added / removed / changed / same. The selftest proves: an
# after-only album appears once as added with its digest (the added law); a before-only album appears once as removed with its digest
# (the removed law); a name in both with a moved digest appears once carrying old and new, an unchanged name is counted same and in no
# list (the changed law); a catalog against itself yields all zeros with same_count equal to the album count (the identity law). A
# pure classification only — no real file, no DAC, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_library_diff_witness.rish

say "ales-library-diff: Language EN — ALES229 names what changed between two catalog versions: classify(before, after) sorts every album into added (after-only), removed (before-only), changed (a name in both whose content-address digest moved), or same — the honest answer to what changed since yesterday's catalog."
say "ales-library-diff: Style Radiant — a diff composes ON the ALES228 resolve rather than re-walking from scratch; the content-address digest is the whole comparison, so no byte compare and no new hash; the added law, the removed law, the changed law, and the identity law each named and proven on metal."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/library_diff"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/library_diff.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-library-diff: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/library_diff.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-library-diff: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-library-diff: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-library-diff' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-library-diff: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-library-diff line"

say "ales-library-diff: GREEN — a keeper sees exactly what moved between two versions of their body of work, and the library level's working set grows a first primitive that stands ON another (find). The next Lotus crux still names who made it — a signed carry (crypto seam) on Keaton's word."
